  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transitional Assistance to IDPs in Erbil, Iraq</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Iraq):  With this additional U.S. assistance, Catholic Relief Services (CRS) Transitional Assistance will expand work under its second strategic objective, which focuses the strengthening of organizational and programming capacities of the Chaldean Archdiocese of Erbil&apos;s nascent NGO, the Ankawa Humanitarian Committee (AHC). The aim is to enable AHC to eventually design, apply and, if successful, implement USG regulations-compliant programs. AHC will also be able to better identify areas of improvement and maximize strengths as they serve the local community and the most vulnerable among them. The capacity strengthening process under this project complements a long-term process led by AHC to continue its growth to become a strong institution. USAID&apos;s funding to AHC will allow it to continue the establishment of necessary policies and institutions, while also enabling the growing organization to test these policies and procedures while designing and implementing activities to help the vulnerable members of their community. This two-pronged approach ensures that the immediate needs of IDPs in Erbil are met, while preparing AHC to be able to self-identify areas for improvement in organization capacity, and work towards a longer-term vision of serving vulnerable groups in the local community. 100% of the funding for this activity is attributable to the Religious and Ethnic Minorities and People-to-People Conflict Prevention and Peace building KIs.</narrative>
  </description>
